Endpoints are unchanged, including six empty records and single-star figures.
No artwork, sector boundaries, or upstream stellar position catalogue is included.
These adapted data retain CC BY-SA 4.0, separately from the package GPL code.

Stellar supplement retrieved 4 November 2026
Contains information from the SIMBAD database, CDS, Strasbourg, France,
available under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0:
https://simbad.cfa.harvard.edu/simbad/
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
Acknowledgement: This work uses the SIMBAD database operated at CDS,
Strasbourg, France. Reference: Wenger et al. (2000), A&AS 143, 9.
https://doi.org/10.1051/aas:2000332
The SIMBAD-derived supplement and its field-reference table retain ODbL 1.0.
The machine-readable supplement, source queries, extraction and conversion
script are supplied in the working source (data-raw/simbad-2026-11-04);
the field-reference table is also installed in ephemeris/.
Additional Johnson V magnitudes: ESA (1997), The Hipparcos and Tycho
Catalogues, ESA SP-1200; CDS/VizieR I/239/hip_main (Vmag).
https://cdsarc.cds.unistra.fr/viz-bin/cat/I/239
VizieR acknowledgement: this work uses the VizieR catalogue access tool,
CDS, Strasbourg, France (DOI: 10.26093/cds/vizier).
These additions were retrieved directly from SIMBAD and VizieR, not NASA.
The supplement adds 59 stellar records and identifies existing 39 Com A as
HIP 63948 without changing that record's numeric values. Other original
catalogue records are unchanged. SIMBAD ICRS coordinates are at epoch J2000;
proper motion in RA includes cos(dec), in mas/year; declination motion is in
mas/year, parallax in mas, radial velocity in km/s. Angles are converted to
sexagesimal only. Hipparcos Vmag is used where SIMBAD has no V magnitude;
Hipparcos J1991.25 positions are NOT copied as J2000 coordinates.
HIP 108797 uses SIMBAD's Hipparcos-2007 measurement-table PM/parallax values
(2007A&A...474..653V), matching the coordinate reference. Five unavailable
radial velocities use explicitly documented zero placeholders, not measured
values: HIP 4714, 51734, 72181, 79634 and 114164. Per-record references,
retrieval date and assumptions are in star-supplement-2026-11-04.csv.
No star position or magnitude was guessed. Missing spectral types remain ~.

Star-name lookup (star.names)
Stellar proper names: International Astronomical Union Working Group on Star
Names, IAU Catalog of Star Names.
https://exopla.net/star-names/modern-iau-star-names/
The 304-entry lookup also contains non-stellar object names. It is distinct
from the astrometric catalogue. The maintainer confirms that he manually transcribed the stellar names
from an IAU table. The exact table version, extraction date and a separate
licence declaration for that compilation are not recorded locally.

Schematic Milky Way outline (extdata/milky-way.csv)
Adapted from diffuse stellar light in Deep Star Maps 2020.
https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/4851/
Credit: NASA/Goddard Space Flight Center Scientific Visualization Studio;
ESA/Gaia/DPAC. This is an illustrative outline, not the source image or a
prediction of visibility. It does not reconstruct the Galaxy's evolution.

